# Exclusions for CrossOver over DXMT (the Steam bottle with CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=dxmt;
# CrossOver 26.3 bundles DXMT v0.72-25-gf35d839, older than Neptune's v0.80-116-g8b9d334
# in dxmt.jsonl).  The D3D10/D3D11 and DXGI binaries only: under this backend D3D12 is
# Wine's vkd3d, and D3D9 is wined3d as in crossover.jsonl.
#   CX_ENV=CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=dxmt ./dxcts run --per-group --exclusion crossover-dxmt
# One flat JSON object per line; "reason" is required.  See docs/exclusions.md.
{"binary": "WGF11SharedResources.exe", "reason": "Carried over from dxmt.jsonl, not rerun: Exhausted host GPU memory on the D3DMetal backend (suites/exclusions/d3dmetal.jsonl: Metal Insufficient Memory, kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory, and a host kernel panic on 2026-09-04).  That was D3DMetal's own allocations, and DXMT shares resources through different code, but the memory builds up across the binary's groups on the host GPU either way, so it is not run to find out: a host GPU fault is a host-panic risk.", "evidence": "dxmt.jsonl; WGF11SharedResources in the full sweeps of 2026-10-15 on Neptune and on CrossOver"}
{"binary": "WGF11Shader5x.exe", "group": "Registers\\Limits\\Temp", "reason": "Carried over from dxmt.jsonl, not rerun: on Neptune's DXMT the worker running this group had Metal command buffers aborted with kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorInvalidResource and the host's GPU-fault watchdog stopped the VM; the group could not be told apart from its two neighbours, so all three are out.  CrossOver's DXMT is an older build, but a host GPU fault is a host-panic risk and is not re-run to find out whether it still faults.", "evidence": "dxmt.jsonl; WGF11Shader5x in the Neptune DXMT full sweep of 2026-10-23: the render-server worker's aborted command buffers at 18:55:55 in the QEMU log, and the watchdog stopping the VM"}
